<!--
  The reBot bolted to its bench, with NO scenery.

  This exists so the clearance gate has geometry to measure against on a
  machine that is driving the real arm, where the simulator's scene (table
  legs, cube, textures, skybox) is neither available nor wanted.

  The arm is bolted to the bench, so the work surface is the plane z=0 by
  construction - that number needs no measurement. The EXTENT is deliberately
  generous (2 m square) because the error is one-sided: a modelled bench
  LARGER than the real one refuses poses that would have been safe out past
  the real edge, while a smaller one leaves a hole the gate does not cover.
  Over-refusing is the direction to err in.

  The slab is 10 cm thick and sits entirely below z=0, so its top face is the
  work surface. contype/conaffinity are 0: nothing here is simulated, the geom
  exists only to be measured against with mj_geomDistance, which works
  regardless.
-->
<mujoco model="rebot_bench">
  <include file="robot.xml" />
  <worldbody>
    <geom name="bench" type="box" size="1.0 1.0 0.05" pos="0 0 -0.05"
          contype="0" conaffinity="0" rgba="0.6 0.45 0.25 0.4" />
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
